WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.785
Arabic, Hebrew, Persian,

2
00:00:02.785 --> 00:00:05.107
and Urdu read right to left,

3
00:00:05.107 --> 00:00:08.624
and most bugs come from CSS
that names physical sides.

4
00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:13.144
General Translation helps you
set dir and lang on the html

5
00:00:13.144 --> 00:00:14.850
element from the active locale.

6
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:19.703
Then replace physical properties
like margin-left with logical

7
00:00:19.703 --> 00:00:21.792
ones like margin-inline-start.

8
00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.484
Flex rows, grid columns,

9
00:00:24.484 --> 00:00:28.594
and text alignment flip
on their own; translateX,

10
00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.903
left, and right do not.

11
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:37.663
In Next.js, the root layout calls
getLocaleDirection from gt-next.

12
00:00:38.063 --> 00:00:41.545
It writes the locale to lang
and the direction to dir.

13
00:00:41.945 --> 00:00:44.498
Your team now ships
Arabic with each release.
